# Uint8Array.from(..) and Float64Array.of(..) construct their receiver, and the look at a body says so and no more. What lies below the classes and above them is still found by every road on which a
# program asks for it: by name, under a key made at run time, up the chain from the class and from an object of it, through a class of the program below one of them, and through @@species.
